---
title: "Organic interface"
note: "Codie's operator: HOST's hand grows into an object, and skin and material become one seamless surface. The object comes with its own surface and sound (bh_interface properties), so picture and soundscape always match. Dial the object and the ending. HOST is your ref image 1; delete (image 1) for text only."
tags: [effects, h3, body_horror, ito]
---
@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic surreal body horror, photorealistic
$host = __bh_host__
$thing = __bh_interface__
$ending = {HOST pulls hard, and the object comes along with the hand as a single piece|the change climbs past the elbow, the arm now the same material to the shoulder|HOST lets go with the other hand, and the fingers of the fused hand move under the surface of the object}

CAST
HOST (image 1): $host

SHOT 10s | push in, slow
HOST rests one hand on $thing, framed from the waist up in a quiet dim room. When HOST tries to lift the hand, the fingers do not come away: at the point of contact the skin has already become $thing.surface, flowing seamlessly into the object with no line where one ends and the other begins. HOST pulls gently, then harder; the joined surface stretches slightly and holds. The change spreads a few centimetres up the wrist in a clean even edge, the skin turning into $thing.surface as it passes. HOST stares at the hand, now visibly part of $thing, and presses the free hand against the boundary. In the final moment $ending.
SFX: quiet room ambience; strained breathing; $thing.sfx; a slow tension as the hand pulls
MUSIC: N/A
